WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.150
Liquid Glass

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.520
bends light.

3
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.240
Yet Apple's showcase proves

4
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.260
pretty UI

5
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.950
can feel slow.

6
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.350
Most teams assume

7
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.750
translucency is harmless.

8
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.950
Instead, live refraction

9
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.020
triggers a strict

10
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.800
400-millisecond race.

11
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.900
A 1982 IBM benchmark

12
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.550
exposes the cost:

13
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.450
latency, and contrast.

14
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.380
Launched at WWDC 2025

15
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.820
for iOS 26

16
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.780
and macOS Tahoe 26,

17
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.700
it adapts visionOS physics.

18
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.050
Static blur softens pixels.

19
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.540
Liquid Glass warps icons

20
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:34.760
under specular curves.

21
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.250
Yet real-time shading

22
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.800
drains GPU headroom.

23
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.680
Both researchers, Walter Doherty

24
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.050
and Ahrvind Thadani,

25
00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:41.950
timed human focus.

26
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.350
Touch feedback needs

27
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.880
under 100 milliseconds.

28
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:45.960
Full flow

29
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.450
demands replies inside

30
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.450
400 milliseconds.

31
00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:49.650
Shader stutters cross

32
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.020
that Doherty Threshold,

33
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:52.000
while busy feeds

34
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.050
bleeding through glass

35
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.450
crush legibility.

36
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.450
Users hesitate,

37
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.960
squinting at washed-out text.

38
00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.750
Confine refraction strictly

39
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.050
to floating navigation

40
00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:00.850
and controls.

41
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.340
Keep dense copy

42
00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.350
on solid cards

43
00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:04.430
so reading stays effortless

44
00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.050
at full speed.

45
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.720
Interfaces earn trust

46
00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.350
only after

47
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.580
they feel instant.

48
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:09.270
Beat the

49
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.020
400-millisecond clock first,

50
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.180
then let your

51
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:12.880
glass shine.
